    "long_instructions": "## Variables, Expressions, and Output\r\n\r\n### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Ask AI Tutor to write a program that:\r\n\r\n   * Stores the number of pizza slices and the number of people in variables\r\n   * Uses an expression to calculate the number of slices per person\r\n   * Builds and prints a message with the result\r\n\r\n2. Run the program and examine AI Tutor’s code.\r\n\r\n3. Use AI Tutor’s code as a model to create your own calculation program. Choose what your program will calculate.\r\n\r\n   Your program must:\r\n\r\n   * Store at least two starting values in variables\r\n   * Use an expression to calculate a result\r\n   * Store the result in a variable\r\n   * Build and print a message that includes the result\r\n\r\n   Your program could calculate a price, distance, time, score, measurement, or something else you choose.\r\n\r\n4. Run your program and fix any errors. You may ask AI Tutor for hints, but do not ask it to write your program for you.",
